## Task 1: Add done_script select dropdown to client_full2.html creation modal

**File:** `server/templates/client_full2.html`

**What:** Add a Done Script select dropdown to the "Create New Idea" modal, between the Description textarea and the button row.

**Approach:** Insert a new `<div>` block after the description field (after line 257, before line 258's button div). Copy the exact pattern from `client_full.html` lines 245-250:

```html
<div style="margin-bottom:1rem">
    <label style="display:block;color:#8b949e;font-size:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.3rem">Done Script (optional)</label>
    <select id="new-idea-done-script" style="width:100%;padding:0.5rem;background:#0d1117;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:4px;color:#c9d1d9;font-size:0.9rem;font-family:inherit">
        <option value="">(none)</option>
    </select>
</div>
```

**Dependencies:** None.

## Task 2: Add fetchScriptsForNewIdea function to client_full2.html

**File:** `server/templates/client_full2.html`

**What:** Add a `fetchScriptsForNewIdea()` function that populates the done_script select dropdown by fetching from the scripts API.

**Approach:** Add the following function in the `<script>` block (after the `showNewIdeaModal` function, around line 613). Copy the pattern from `client_full.html` lines 567-578:

```javascript
function fetchScriptsForNewIdea() {
    var scriptSelect = document.getElementById('new-idea-done-script');
    scriptSelect.innerHTML = '<option value="">(none)</option>';
    fetch('/api/clients/' + encodeURIComponent(_clientID) + '/scripts?key=' + encodeURIComponent(_dashKey)).then(function(r) { return r.json(); }).then(function(scripts) {
        scripts.forEach(function(s) {
            var opt = document.createElement('option');
            opt.value = s.id;
            opt.textContent = s.label;
            scriptSelect.appendChild(opt);
        });
    }).catch(function() {});
}
```

**Dependencies:** Task 1 (the select element must exist).

## Task 3: Update showNewIdeaModal to reset done_script and fetch scripts

**File:** `server/templates/client_full2.html`

**What:** Modify the `showNewIdeaModal()` function to reset the done_script select and call `fetchScriptsForNewIdea()`.

**Approach:** In `showNewIdeaModal()` (line 603-612):
1. After line 607 (`document.getElementById('new-idea-description').value = '';`), add:
   ```javascript
   document.getElementById('new-idea-done-script').value = '';
   ```
2. Before or after `document.getElementById('new-idea-title').focus();` (line 612), add:
   ```javascript
   fetchScriptsForNewIdea();
   ```

**Dependencies:** Tasks 1 and 2.

## Task 4: Update submitNewIdea to include done_script in POST body

**File:** `server/templates/client_full2.html`

**What:** Modify the `submitNewIdea()` function to read the done_script value and include it in the POST request body.

**Approach:**
1. After line 622 (`var description = ...`), add:
   ```javascript
   var doneScript = document.getElementById('new-idea-done-script').value;
   ```
2. Change line 640 from:
   ```javascript
   body: JSON.stringify({title: title, board: board, description: description})
   ```
   to:
   ```javascript
   body: JSON.stringify({title: title, board: board, description: description, done_script: doneScript})
   ```

**Dependencies:** Task 1.

## Task 5: Increase TUI NewFeatureModal max-height

**File:** `pipeline/tui.py`

**What:** Increase the `max-height` of the `#new-dialog` container in `NewFeatureModal` so all fields (including Done Script) are visible on smaller terminals. Also make the container scrollable.

**Approach:** In the CSS block of `NewFeatureModal` (line 858), change:
```css
max-height: 28;
```
to:
```css
max-height: 36;
```

This provides enough room for all widgets: Label (New Item) + Board label+select + Type label+select + Title label+input + Description label+input + Done Script label+select + Buttons = ~7 widget groups × ~4 lines each (with margins) ≈ 28-32 lines. A max-height of 36 gives comfortable headroom.

Alternatively, add `overflow-y: auto;` to `#new-dialog` to make it scrollable if contents exceed the height:
```css
#new-dialog {
    width: 70;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 36;
    overflow-y: auto;
    border: thick $panel;
    background: $surface;
    padding: 1 2;
}
```

**Dependencies:** None.

## Summary of files modified

1. `server/templates/client_full2.html` — Tasks 1-4 (add done_script select, fetch function, wire into modal open/submit)
2. `pipeline/tui.py` — Task 5 (increase modal max-height)

## Testing Notes

- **WebUI (client_full2):** Open a client page, click "+ New Idea", verify the Done Script dropdown appears and is populated with scripts from the API. Create an idea with a done_script selected and verify the feature JSON file has the done_script field set.
- **TUI:** Launch the TUI, press 'n' to open the New Item modal, verify the Done Script select is visible without scrolling on a standard 80×24 terminal. Verify creating an item with a done_script works correctly.
